                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "In 1979, an aluminum smelter on Cornwall Island released roughly 300 tons of fluoride a year. Within five miles, cattle herds collapsed — skeletal fluorosis, lameness, tooth loss, starvation. That historical case raises questions about forage exposure, but it does not establish the outcome at Inola. The revised September proposal cannot be compared with it using the earlier annual estimate.",
